        "original_id": "92e51764-e4bc-536a-9536-63da7cf95423",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kim Wilson, Chino Moreno, Colin James, Sergio Vega\n- Bands and Projects: The Fabulous Thunderbirds, Deftones, Team Sleep, Crosses, Saudade, Palms\n- Songs and Works: \"Tuff Enuff\", \"Wrap It Up\", \"Tempest\", My Kind Of Evil\n- Topics: music careers, band roles, production credits\n\nFacts:\n- Kim Wilson is best known as the lead vocalist and frontman for The Fabulous Thunderbirds on the 1980s hit songs \"Tuff Enuff\" and \"Wrap It Up.\"\n- Chino Moreno was born as Camillo Wong Moreno on June 20, 1973, and he is an American musician.\n- Chino Moreno is best known as the lead vocalist and contributing guitarist of Deftones.\n- Chino Moreno is also a member of the side-project groups Team Sleep, Crosses, Saudade, and Palms.\n- My Kind Of Evil was produced by multi-Grammy nominee Kim Wilson, who is a singer for The Fabulous Thunderbirds, and it features fellow Canadian Colin James on two tracks.\n- The song \"Tempest\" debuted on PureVolume's official website on October 3, 2012, with a video featuring Deftones members Chino Moreno and Sergio Vega discussing the track.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ef12a14a-d31b-50fc-83b4-acf498ca75f2",
        "text": "Page: Kim Wilson. Sentence: He is best known as the lead vocalist and frontman for the Fabulous Thunderbirds on two hit songs of the 1980s, \"Tuff Enuff\" and \"Wrap It Up.\"\nPage: Chino Moreno. Sentence: Chino Moreno (born Camillo Wong Moreno; June 20, 1973) is an American musician.\nPage: Chino Moreno. Sentence: He is best known as the lead vocalist and contributing guitarist of Deftones.\nPage: Chino Moreno. Sentence: He is also a member of the side-project groups Team Sleep, Crosses, Saudade, and Palms.\nPage: My Kind Of Evil. Sentence: It was produced by multi-Grammy nominee Kim Wilson (singer for The Fabulous Thunderbirds) and features fellow Canadian Colin James on two tracks.\nPage: Tempest (Deftones song). Sentence: The song debuted on PureVolume's official website on October 3, 2012 along with a video featuring band members Chino Moreno and Sergio Vega giving some insight regarding the track.",
